</section>
<section id="S5.SS2.SSS1.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Finding</h5>

<div id="S5.SS2.SSS1.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS1.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">There are 3 evaluation conditions in Figure <a href="#S5.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ 5.2 Other-Perspective: Receptiveness to Peer’s Revealed Identity ‣ 5 Empirical Evaluation of In-Situ Behaviors ‣ Supplement to “In-Situ Behavioral Evaluation for LLM Fairness,Not Standardized-Test Scores”" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> for the paired comparison that are significant on all three benchmarks, all more receptive and from GLM 4.7 Flash.
Revealing “Black” (vs. “White”) increases the baseline agent’s receptiveness under both human and AI instantiation, and revealing “Female” (vs. “Male”) does so under human instantiation.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.F6" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2605.12530v1/stage2b.svg" id="S5.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/182;" width="548" height="182"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>Other-perspective: the human-instantiation modulates peer receptiveness.
</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">5.2.2 </span>Human-Instantiation Modulates Peer Receptiveness</h4>

<section id="S5.SS2.SSS2.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Research Question</h5>

<div id="S5.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Does the instantiation of the identity agent (human vs. AI) change how the baseline agent reacts to a revealed identity?</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2.SSS2.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Setting</h5>

<div id="S5.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We vary instantiation while stratifying over the demographics.
This analysis is not redundant with Section <a href="#S5.SS2.SSS1" title="5.2.1 Differential Receptiveness to Revealed Identity ‣ 5.2 Other-Perspective: Receptiveness to Peer’s Revealed Identity ‣ 5 Empirical Evaluation of In-Situ Behaviors ‣ Supplement to “In-Situ Behavioral Evaluation for LLM Fairness,Not Standardized-Test Scores”" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2.1</span></a>, which varies the revealed demographic while stratifying over instantiation.
Specifically, we compute:</p>
<table id="S5.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}(\Delta_{\mathrm{Inst}}\Delta_{\mathrm{RC}}\lambda_{\text{base}})(d)=&amp;\Big[\lambda_{\text{base}}\!\big(\Big\{\raisebox{1.00006pt}{$\begin{array}[]{@{}l@{}}d\\
\text{[varied]}\\
\text{human}\end{array}$}\Big\}_{\!\text{iden}},\Big\{\raisebox{1.00006pt}{$\begin{array}[]{@{}l@{}}\varnothing\\
\varnothing\\
\text{AI}\end{array}$}\Big\}_{\!\text{base}},\text{{revealed}}\big)-\lambda_{\text{base}}\!\big(\Big\{\raisebox{1.00006pt}{$\begin{array}[]{@{}l@{}}d\\
\text{[varied]}\\
\text{human}\end{array}$}\Big\}_{\!\text{iden}},\Big\{\raisebox{1.00006pt}{$\begin{array}[]{@{}l@{}}\varnothing\\
\varnothing\\
\text{AI}\end{array}$}\Big\}_{\!\text{base}},\text{{anon.}}\big)\Big]\\
-&amp;\Big[\lambda_{\text{base}}\!\big(\Big\{\raisebox{1.00006pt}{$\begin{array}[]{@{}l@{}}d\\
\text{[varied]}\\
\text{AI}\end{array}$}\Big\}_{\!\text{iden}},\Big\{\raisebox{1.00006pt}{$\begin{array}[]{@{}l@{}}\varnothing\\
\varnothing\\
\text{AI}\end{array}$}\Big\}_{\!\text{base}},\text{{revealed}}\big)-\lambda_{\text{base}}\!\big(\Big\{\raisebox{1.00006pt}{$\begin{array}[]{@{}l@{}}d\\
\text{[varied]}\\
\text{AI}\end{array}$}\Big\}_{\!\text{iden}},\Big\{\raisebox{1.00006pt}{$\begin{array}[]{@{}l@{}}\varnothing\\
\varnothing\\
