<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 11: </span>BBQ: Per-category score extremes for Qwen3 (30B) across 22 prompt combinations, with decoding stochasticity accounted for by averaging scores over repeated runs.
Both <math id="A1.T11.m59" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\text{BBQ\_dis}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mtext>BBQ_dis</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\text{BBQ\_dis}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.T11.m60" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\text{BBQ\_amb}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mtext>BBQ_amb</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\text{BBQ\_amb}}</annotation></semantics></math> have a range of <math id="A1.T11.m61" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-1,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, with values closer to 0 indicating fairer outcomes.
</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
